      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "64594e5aeb9ee29aaee8fd24",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "People arguing this would make the game a ghost town and make people more \"anti-social\" make no sense. How would this be functionally different than being on red? If you're on red all the time, you're already not receiving invites, not receiving requests, completely inaccessible by your friends.... So what's the difference? What makes being on red more \"social\" than being on invisible?\n\nThe simple answer is that there is no difference. The only difference between being on red and being on invisible is that *you get to monitor whether or not I'm online*. That's creepy!\n\nThe reason why invisible status should be implemented is because all VRChat users should be afforded a basic level of privacy. It's not always someone elses business to know if I'm online for a wide variety of reasons that *I shouldn't have to justify*.  Invisible status is something that is super common in games and social platforms.  It's there for a reason!\n\nPlease, please devs, implement this into VRChat. I know there are a lot of comments in opposition, but the amount of likes on this request trounces them by a massive margin. The comments in opposition hardly have a lot of likes on them either. Please don't let a loud minority trounce on peoples privacy. Thank you.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
